  "findings": "Compared small rounded evergreen leaves and dense shrub form photographs, then all current three-size pilots and 36 variants. The displayed Fastigiata cultivar was excluded from the natural silhouette decision; the hedge photograph informs density rather than clipping. Added numerous fine terminal shoots, thinner green young twigs and smaller main stems after the first pilot looked brown and bare. Current irregular untrimmed outlines span 1.15-2.42 m and retain dense twig-following leaf cover without spherical blobs. Opposite phyllotaxy and tiny spring flowers are not individually legible at 25 mm; the source is accepted as a stylized natural box shrub, with user variant endorsement separate.",
